{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1468099-demiplane-announces-wod5-digital-platform","id":1468099,"title":"Demiplane announces WOD5 digital platform","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-16T22:38:44-08:00","id":1468099,"title":"Demiplane announces WOD5 digital platform","content":"Coming 2022 from the creators of DnD Beyond, and Pathfinder Nexus &quot;World of Darkness Nexus&quot; will offer rulebooks and lore compendiums, PC management, Session management tools and even a Roll20-like voice option, supporting V5, W5 and H5<br /> <br /> Who else is thrilled? The adoption of CHRONICA-style features and of in-built voice and video options is definitely interesting. <br /> <br /> I'm curios about rules and lore compendium, WOD books are usually different in format from D&amp;D rulebooks and adventure books: will we buy &quot;Chicago by Night&quot;, unlocking rules and a library of NPCs, or will we have native contents? <br /> <br /> I'm happy, I really liked the PC and Chronicle management option of the &quot; New, Old&quot; World of Darkness website whicj were scrapped after Paradox absorbed WW again<br /> This looks like that idea on steroids: I hope we get also support for LARPs. <br /> <br /> Official trailer: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/F8T-PJVWO_8\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/F8T-PJVWO_8</a><br /> <br /> Website: <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarknessnexus.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarknessnexus.com/</a><br /> <br /> A piece of news: <a href=\"https://www.geeknative.com/136729/world-of-darkness-nexus-announced-as-official-vtt-and-digital-toolset-for-vampire-werewolf-and-hunter/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.geeknative.com/136729/wo...lf-and-hunter/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachm